{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837974",
      "title": "Resetting Forms",
      "sourceHash": "0e02208fb2bb0258fd4ed5a2518eac212a3cd1996c88f49f2d59d0d8991f0dff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 1.62,
          "en": "So now that we learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.62,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "about different strategies for getting the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 7.95,
          "en": "the next step typically of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.95,
          "end": 12.45,
          "en": "is to also validate that input to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "that it's correct and we got all the data we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "But before we'll actually dive into that part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 25.97,
          "en": "I briefly want to explore how we can reset such a form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 28.89,
          "en": "Now for that, on that form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 31.863,
          "en": "we for example got that Reset button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 37.02,
          "en": "And indeed, if I enter some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.02,
          "end": 40.53,
          "en": "into my form here into any input fields of my choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.53,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "and I then click on this Reset button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 48.36,
          "en": "The form indeed is reset and those inputs are cleared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.36,
          "end": 51.96,
          "en": "And that's happening because in that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 56.96,
          "en": "on that reset button, the type attribute is set to reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.28,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "And that's one of the built-in types we can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 67.55,
          "en": "We got button, submit and reset, submit is the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.35,
          "en": "And of course, well submits the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "button is a value we explored before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 76.62,
          "en": "It allows this button to act as a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.62,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "that does not submit the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "and that also doesn't do anything else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 86.61,
          "en": "And the last value reset, therefore is the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 87.84,
          "en": "you wanna choose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.84,
          "end": 92.78999999999999,
          "en": "If you have a button in a form that should reset that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.78999999999999,
          "end": 95.37299999999999,
          "en": "So that's one way of resetting it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 100.233,
          "en": "Another way is to programmatically reset it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 105.50999999999999,
          "en": "Now for that, if you are managing the input with state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 110.50999999999999,
          "en": "You can of course simply reset those state values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "For example, here in that state login component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 118.17,
          "en": "we worked on before, we could set the entered values state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 123.15,
          "en": "to that same object we used as an initial state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 128.15,
          "en": "Where email and password both have empty strings as values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 129.24,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "And since those values are then set as values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 135.57,
          "en": "on those inputs, those state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "would be reflected there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 141.21,
          "en": "So that's how you can reset input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 144.69,
          "en": "when managing those values via state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "Now, when getting the entered values with refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 153.11,
          "en": "you can reset the inputs by manually setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 157.65,
          "en": "the value property of the connected input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 157.65,
          "end": 159.42000000000002,
          "en": "to empty strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 159.42000000000002,
          "end": 163.17000000000002,
          "en": "But this is a solution you should use with care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 163.17000000000002,
          "end": 166.44,
          "en": "because typically you should leave it up to React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 166.44,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "to update the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 172.26,
          "en": "And you should not imperatively perform updates or changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 172.26,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "It might be just a small update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 177.84,
          "en": "but it is an update to the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.84,
          "end": 180.183,
          "en": "and therefore not really recommended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.02,
          "end": 183.78,
          "en": "Instead here when working with refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 187.56,
          "en": "it's typically better to reset the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.56,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "as you also can do it when using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "that foreign data approach for extracting the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "Because in that handleSubmit function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "we're getting this event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 201.32999999999998,
          "en": "And as I already mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.32999999999998,
          "end": 205.563,
          "en": "the target of that event is the underlying form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.55,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "And it turns out that this form element has a reset method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 212.253,
          "en": "which you can call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.09,
          "end": 217.41,
          "en": "Which is essentially the same thing this button does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 217.41,
          "end": 221.133,
          "en": "if you set the type to reset as I'm doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.9,
          "end": 226.98,
          "en": "So calling reset on event target is another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 228.87,
          "en": "of clearing that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 230.76,
          "en": "And yes, if we're honest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.76,
          "end": 233.76,
          "en": "this is also some imperative code again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 233.76,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "but at least it's less code to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "then resetting all those ref values manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 243.84,
          "en": "by setting them back to empty strings step by step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.84,
          "end": 247.92,
          "en": "That's why you should prefer this event target reset code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 247.92,
          "end": 251.073,
          "en": "over manually resetting all the ref values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 254.94,
          "en": "And with that, we now, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.94,
          "end": 259.35,
          "en": "can make sure that if we submit the form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 259.35,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "we also reset that when clicking Sign up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 265.08299999999997,
          "en": "Thanks to calling reset here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 268.83,
          "en": "Now here, I actually don't wanna reset the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.83,
          "end": 271.8,
          "en": "but of course it is important to know how you could do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 274.86,
          "en": "and now you know and therefore now we're ready",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.86,
          "end": 276.483,
          "en": "to dive into validation.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}